mothershipOS: after waiting on the PCM's poll descriptors, let alsa-lib translate the events
(snd_pcm_poll_descriptors_revents). Plugin devices (ioplug: the PipeWire ALSA plugin) update their state in that
call; without it the stream took one period and then the backend never saw room again: the guest kept playing and
the host got silence. A hw device or dmix does not need it, which is why the DisplayPort path worked.

--- a/src/audio_backends/alsa.rs
+++ b/src/audio_backends/alsa.rs
@@ -494,6 +494,8 @@
                     lck.get()?
                 };
                 alsa::poll::poll(&mut fds, 100)?;
+                let lck = pcm.lock().unwrap();
+                let _ = lck.revents(&fds);
             }
         }
     }
